IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-seat`
IMPORT `je54-seat-powers-and-penalties`

-- je54-tests-independent: an independent test author's answers to scenarios on the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 (L.17/1954).
--
-- STATUS: every expected value in this file is "assumed, not ruled".
-- It is one reader's reading of the deposited texts.  Nobody with authority has ruled on any reading.
-- Most expected values were decided from the seven texts of the Law (and, for commencement around 28 September 2021 only,
-- Articles 3(2) and 3(6) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) BEFORE the encoding was opened, and were written down in
-- decisions.md in the author's scratch directory; their IDs (A01, E03, ...) are the IDs of that file.  CORRECTED AFTER THE RUN: a few dozen scenarios (every ID with a letter suffix, such as N10b or P13b, and some others) were added while this file was being written, AFTER the exported names and the "some other ..." options had been read, and are not in decisions.md; the O09 below is not the O09 of decisions.md.
-- The encoding's exported names were read afterwards, to learn how to call them; no expected value was changed after a run, and the only change to this file after the run is this comment and the O09 label.
-- SPLIT.  Part 3 of 3 of the independent test pass, cut by Article after the run so that no file passes about 600 lines: Articles 9 to 11A, Articles 16 and 17 and the Schedule Part 1; sections M, N, P, R.
-- The header and the Helpers section are repeated in each part.  No assertion was altered, deleted or moved to another section; the 520 assertions of the original are the 520 across the three parts.
--
-- VERSIONS.  V1 = l_17_1954_20210927 (1 Jan 2019 to 27 Sep 2021); V2a = l_17_1954_20220130 (28 Sep 2021 to 30 Jan 2022);
-- V2b = l_17_1954_20220831 (31 Jan to 31 Aug 2022); V2c = l_17_1954_20240110 (1 Sep 2022 to 10 Jan 2024);
-- V2d = l_17_1954_20251123 (11 Jan 2024 to 23 Nov 2025); V2e = l_17_1954_20260618 (24 Nov 2025 to 18 Jun 2026);
-- V2f = l_17_1954.current (19 Jun 2026 to current).  "V1 src:9" means line 9 of the V1 text, and so on for each version.
--
-- CLOSED OR SILENT.  Where the Law gives a closed answer a negative is FALSE.  Where the Law is silent the answer is a refusal.
-- Where an Article carries "unless the contrary intention appears" (or the context, or, in Article 11A, "the contrary is expressed")
-- and the input says it does appear, the Law says only that its own construction does not apply, never what applies instead:
-- the answer is a refusal, not FALSE.  Where an Article carries no such qualifier (13(2), for one) the input has no effect.
-- The text of a refusal is not asserted except for dates before 1 January 2019, whose message the brief fixes.
--
-- COMMENCEMENT.  An enactment "expressed to come into operation on a particular day" comes into operation "immediately on the
-- expiration of the previous day" (V1 Art 1(5), V1 src:9), that is at the start of that day.  One that is silent or says forthwith
-- is construed as expressed to come into operation on the day it was passed or made (V1 Art 1(6), V1 src:10), so, read together,
-- at the start of that day, even though that is before it was made.  The moment asserted is the start of the day on the clock of
-- the zone named (Etc/UTC unless said); the Law names no zone.

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment expresses the time of its commencement`
      named IS A MAYBE DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`stated as` how named made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS how
        `the day it names` IS named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment expresses the time of its commencement`
      named IS A MAYBE DATE
      made IS A DATE
      asked IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`stated as and asked on` how named made asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS how
        `the day it names` IS named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS JUST asked

`reading by commencement` MEANS `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
`reading by day made` MEANS `the day the enactment was passed or made`
`reading by day asked` MEANS `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`UTC moment` y mo d h mi s MEANS DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A DATE
`day of commencement` c r MEANS (`on what day did the enactment come into force` c r)'s `the day`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A `Basis of a reading`
`basis of commencement` c r MEANS (`on what day did the enactment come into force` c r)'s `the basis`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      zone IS A STRING
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A DATETIME
`moment of commencement` c zone r MEANS (`at what moment did the enactment come into force` c zone r)'s `the moment`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in force at the UTC moment` c y mo d h mi s MEANS
    (`was the enactment in force at a moment` (`UTC moment` y mo d h mi s) "Etc/UTC" c `reading by commencement`)'s `the answer`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in force on the day` c d MEANS
    (`was the enactment in force on a day` d c `reading by commencement`)'s `the answer`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Local moment`
`local moment` d h mi s MEANS
    `Local moment` WITH
        `calendar day` IS d
        `hour of the day` IS h
        `minute of the hour` IS mi
        `second of the minute` IS s

GIVEN m IS A `Local moment`
      d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local moment is` m d h mi s MEANS
    m's `calendar day` EQUALS d AND m's `hour of the day` EQUALS h AND m's `minute of the hour` EQUALS mi AND m's `second of the minute` EQUALS s

§ `M. Articles 9 and 10`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of division referred to`
      number IS A STRING
      more IS A BOOLEAN
      holder IS A `Kind of instrument`
      law IS A STRING
      division IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Reference by number or letter`
`reference` kind number more holder law division MEANS
    `Reference by number or letter` WITH
        `the kind of division named` IS kind
        `the number or letter given` IS number
        `further identification is given` IS more
        `the kind of instrument that contains the reference` IS holder
        `the instrument that contains the reference` IS law
        `the division that contains the reference` IS division

-- M01  V1 src:41: in Law X, "Article 5" by number only is Article 5 of Law X
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `an Article` "5" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2"))'s `the kind of division` EQUALS `an Article`
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `an Article` "5" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "5"
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `an Article` "5" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2"))'s `the place it is in` EQUALS "Law X"
-- M02  V1 src:41: "Schedule 2" and "Part 3" likewise
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `a Schedule` "2" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2"))'s `the kind of division` EQUALS `a Schedule`
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `a Part` "3" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "3"
-- M03  V1 src:41 "without further identification": "Article 5 of the Companies Law" is not within 9(1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `an Article` "5" TRUE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 2")
-- M05  V1 src:42: in Article 8 of Law X, "paragraph (3)" by number only is paragraph (3) of Article 8
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `a paragraph` "(3)" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 8"))'s `the kind of division` EQUALS `a paragraph`
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `a paragraph` "(3)" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 8"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "(3)"
-- M06  V1 src:42: a sub-paragraph by letter only
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `a sub-paragraph` "(b)" FALSE `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "Law X" "Article 8"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "(b)"
-- M14  V1 src:44: regulations made under a Law, "Article 3" by number only: Article 3 of those regulations
#ASSERT (`where does the reference by number or letter lead` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`reference` `an Article` "3" FALSE `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` "the X Regulations" "Article 1"))'s `the number or letter` EQUALS "3"
-- M08  V1 src:43: a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to it as amended from time to time
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the enactment as amended` FALSE
-- M09  V1 src:43: and as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the enactment as extended or applied under another enactment` FALSE
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the enactment as extended or applied under another provision of the same Law` FALSE
-- M10  V1 src:43 "unless the context otherwise requires"
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the enactment as amended` TRUE
-- M11  V2b src:41: as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2022 3 1) `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2022 3 1) `the enactment as amended` FALSE
-- M12  V1: revised or consolidated is not dealt with (see A17)
#ASSERT REFUSED `is the reference to an enactment a reference to it in this form` (YMD 2021 6 1) `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
