GIVEN vacant IS A BOOLEAN
      removed IS A BOOLEAN
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      incapacitated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Circumstances of an office`
`office circumstances` vacant removed absent incapacitated MEANS
    `Circumstances of an office` WITH
        `the office is vacant` IS vacant
        `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office` IS removed
        `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently` IS absent
        `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance` IS incapacitated

`office in good order` MEANS `office circumstances` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- N25  V2b src:54 (1)(a): a power to appoint to an office includes power to determine the terms and conditions of appointment
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N26  V2b src:55 (1)(b): to remove or suspend
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N27  V2b src:56 (1)(c): to reappoint or reinstate
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to reappoint or reinstate a person to the office` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N28  V2b src:57, src:59 (1)(d) with (2)(a): to appoint in place of the last holder where the office is vacant
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` (`office circumstances` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
-- N29-N30  V2b src:60 (2)(b): the holder has been removed or suspended
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` (`office circumstances` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
-- N31-N32  V2b src:61 (2)(c): the holder is absent temporarily or permanently
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` (`office circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
-- N33  V2b src:62 (2)(d): the holder is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` (`office circumstances` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) FALSE
-- N34-N35  V2b src:57: none of the four circumstances (holder in office and able; or incapacitated without affecting performance): the replacement power is not included
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` `office in good order` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- N36  V2b src:53 "unless the contrary is expressed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `office in good order` TRUE
-- N37  a contrary merely implied is not "expressed": the input stays FALSE, and the related power is included
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N42  11A(1) is engaged only where the enactment confers power to appoint to an office
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) FALSE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N42b  a related power that is not on the list
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2022 3 1) TRUE `some other power` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N39-N40  V2f src:55-64: the same
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` (`office circumstances` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE
#ASSERT `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` `office in good order` FALSE
-- N38 / N41  V1 has no Article 11A; no text before 2019
#ASSERT REFUSED `does the power to appoint to an office include this related power` (YMD 2018 12 31) TRUE `to remove or suspend a person from the office` `office in good order` FALSE

§ `P. Articles 16 and 17 (V1 only)`

-- P01  V1 src:71: a Law passed 2020-03-01 (after the commencement of this Law), to come into operation 2020-06-01, confers power to make regulations; exercised 2020-04-01 as necessary for bringing it into operation
#ASSERT `may the power be exercised before the Law comes into force` (YMD 2020 4 1) `a Law passed after the commencement of the Law` (YMD 2020 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2020 4 1) TRUE FALSE
-- P02  exercised 2020-02-28, before the passing: the Article says "at any time after the passing"
