§ `R. The Schedule, Part 1: "shall mean" is exhaustive, "includes" is not`

`reach within` MEANS `within the word, as the Schedule says`
`reach outside` MEANS `outside the word, because the Schedule says means`
`reach own meaning` MEANS `not named by the Schedule, which says includes and so does not shut it out: the word's own meaning decides`
`reach condition unmet` MEANS `the definition does not apply: the condition it states is not met`

-- word, day, whether the definition names the thing, whether the condition it states (if any) is met; no contrary intention; the Magistrate reading at its default
GIVEN w IS A STRING
      d IS A DATE
      named IS A BOOLEAN
      cond IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reach of a defined expression`
`schedule says` w d named cond MEANS
    `what does the Schedule definition do for the word` w d named cond FALSE `the named things are all that the word covers`

-- R01-R03  V1 src:94: "advocate" shall mean a person admitted to the Bar as an advocate of the Royal Court
#ASSERT `schedule says` "advocate" (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `reach within`
#ASSERT `schedule says` "advocate" (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `reach outside`
